# The fixture filesystem icheck's b6sim cases walk -- task C4e.
#
# WHY THIS IS NOT ../../df/test/fsimg.img.  df's fixture is 200 blocks and its largest file
# is three blocks, all DIRECT -- its own manifest says so, and says that the gap was left for
# this program to fill.  icheck is the only thing on this system that walks an inode's whole
# address list, so a fixture whose files never leave di_addr[0..5] would leave the interesting
# half of it untested: NADDR is 8 and NLEVEL is 2, and v7's `NADDR-3' arithmetic would have
# read di_addr[5] -- a direct block -- as a block of addresses.
#
# /huge IS 519 BLOCKS, AND 519 IS THE POINT.  Six direct addresses cover logical blocks 0..5
# and the single indirect covers 6..517 (NINDIR is 512), so 518 is the first block that can
# only be reached through the DOUBLE indirect.  At 519 data blocks the file has exactly one
# block under the second level, which is the smallest file that makes icheck's `ii=' column
# non-zero -- and the smallest thing in this tree that has ever exercised a double indirect
# at all.  The volume is 600 blocks so that there is still a free list worth salvaging.
#
# The blocks icheck then charges for the file are 519 data + 1 single indirect + 1 double
# indirect + 1 second-level indirect = 522, which is arithmetic the .expected states.
#
# The `source' paths resolve against b6fsutil's working directory, which is this test's build
# directory -- ../../df/test/fsimg.manifest's arrangement, and the reason icheckimg.d/ is
# generated into the build tree.  Nothing binary is checked in.

default
owner 0
group 0
dirmode 0755
filemode 0644

dir /d

file /huge
source icheckimg.d/huge

file /small
source icheckimg.d/small

file /d/nested
source icheckimg.d/small
